kind how-do-i
title How do I show a terminal on a display, and type into it from a keyboard?
intro A path joins a display, a terminal and an input device. vtium writes it as rules that name the display and the keyboard, and the terminal they reach.

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
device display HDMI-A-1 GSM:0x5b88:LEFT0001
device keyboard 046d:c31c USB Keyboard

1. Go to the Flow tab.
note The Flow tab lists the connected displays and input devices under PARTS. NEW PATH collects the parts of the path you are making.
2. Highlight HDMI-A-1.
3. Press Space to pick.
4. Highlight USB Keyboard.
5. Press Space to pick.
note NEW PATH now holds the display and the keyboard, and makes a new terminal for them.
6. Press a to add path.
7. Press s to save.
at the save
check draft display HDMI-A-1 reaches terminal-1
check draft input USB Keyboard reaches terminal-1
